@props(title: text)
<article class="article-page"><a class="text-link" href="/">← Back to the workbench</a><div class="eyebrow">THE SHAPE OF THE EXPERIMENT</div><h1>Less between<br>you and <em>the page.</em></h1><p class="article-lede">A native server, compiled HTML templates, and small browser modules. Three separate jobs. One small framework. Styled with Tailwind CSS, compiled at build time.</p><div class="principles"><section><span>01 / NATIVE</span><h2>Axon renders the page.</h2><p>Templates compile into ordinary Axon functions. The deployed Linux server uses direct kernel calls, without a C runtime or JavaScript engine.</p></section><section><span>02 / OPTIONAL</span><h2>JavaScript adds behavior.</h2><p>The counter and filter load their own modules. Enhanced forms fetch HTML from Axon. Normal links and forms remain useful without JavaScript.</p></section><section><span>03 / PORTABLE</span><h2>A static site is a folder.</h2><p>The same render functions produce exported HTML. This page is prerendered and ships no JavaScript when opened directly.</p></section></div><p class="article-note">This is a v0.1 prototype: GET routes and forms, one shared layout, typed template props, and a small component system. It is not a React runtime or a Next.js compatibility layer.</p></article>
